      "statusChangeID": "6883d2a842a02fdf92fe2480",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This is intended behavior. Animators are expensive to run, so we cull any that you can't see. When culled, animators do not run.\n\nYou should design your animators so that they are deterministic, meaning the animator will always resolve to the correct state based solely on the current values of its parameters, regardless of animation history or transitions. This ensures that when the animator resumes after being culled, it will resolve to the appropriate state automatically.\n\nAnimators that rely on transitional state (e.g. timing-based transitions, trigger chaining, or entry-to-next logic) can desynchronize when culled, since those transitions are not processed while off-screen. If you need a particular state to be active under specific conditions, drive it directly with parameters and use direct transitions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
